    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d813">

                <pb facs="1277" n="1263" xml:id="pg1263"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 E.W./11–2344: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Huddle</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bern</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-11-23T16:00:00+01:00">November 23,
                            1944—4 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 8:53 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>7702. Message contained [in] Department’s 3604, October 23 delivered October 25
                    Swiss Foreign Office which replies in note November 17 stating that Swiss
                    Legation, Berlin, instructed communicate message German Government. When this
                    instruction received Swiss Legation, Berlin, had just suffered on part German
                    Foreign Office two refusals accept communications from United States Government
                    (see Legation’s 7542 November 15<anchor n="57" xml:id="d813-f1"/> and 766 [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">7668</hi>], November 21<anchor n="58" xml:id="d813-f2"
                    />) and as refusal accept Department’s 3604 appeared inevitable it reported
                    situation to Swiss Foreign Office. After examining question in effort find
                    notwithstanding this situation means transmit to German Government Department’s
                    message, Foreign Office, Bern, submitted it under cover of note to German
                    Legation, Bern, which has returned Department’s communication with following
                    remark: “Wording has been chosen by Department of State which would oblige
                    German Foreign Office refuse accept communication.”</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Huddle</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
